course: dictionary
lesson: 10238
title: Toil: hard work and effort
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Toil is a word you may meet in old stories, history books and songs. Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «Goodman Joseph toiled through the snow» tells you he was pushing on through deep snow with great effort, not strolling along.
explain: Toil means to work very hard for a long time, usually at tiring work. In history lessons, people toiled in fields, mines and factories. The clues are the places: fields, mines and factories are where people worked hard and got tired. Try your meaning in the sentence: "people worked very hard in the mines" makes sense.
explain: Toil can also mean moving slowly with great effort, as in «toil up a hill». You can use toil as a noun too: «years of toil» means years of hard, tiring work. When you are not sure, swap in "hard work" or "struggle" and check if the sentence still fits.
fact: Toil is a verb (toil, toils, toiled, toiling) and a noun.
fact: «Toil» means to work very hard for a long time, usually at tiring work.
fact: «Toil» can mean to move slowly with great effort, as in «toil up a hill».
fact: As a noun, toil means hard, tiring work, as in «years of toil». It is uncountable, so we do not say "a toil".
fact: Old meaning: toils (plural) means nets or traps, as in «caught in the toils».
exercise: «Goodman Joseph toiled through the snow.» What does toiled mean here? | Built a warm fire | *Moved on with great effort | Slept soundly | Sang a happy song
exercise: «The people toiled in the fields and mines.» What does toiled mean? | Rested under the trees | Played games all day | Ran quickly to school | *Worked very hard for a long time
exercise: In «years of toil», what is toil? | *Hard, tiring work | A kind of bird | A light holiday | Sleeping and dreaming
test: Ella says, «Toil means to relax on the beach.» Is she right? Use the words around toil to decide. | Yes, toil means to relax | *No, toil means to work hard | Toil means to cook | Toil means to sing
test: In an old story, someone is «caught in the toils». What are toils? | Tall trees | Warm blankets | *Nets or traps | Happy songs
exam: Read «toil up a hill» and «years of toil». Which two meanings of toil do these show? | *Moving slowly with great effort, and hard, tiring work | Sleeping and dreaming | Eating and drinking | Playing and laughing
